{"entity":"story","version":1,"id":"kernel-identity-and-hashing","revision":1,"type":"aep.entity.create/v1","from_state":null,"to_state":"draft","changed":{"body":"## Context\n\nDesign § 6.4 and § 10: human-readable names are not identities; every persistent object carries a\nstable id that survives renames, aliases, merges and schema migration. Design § 57: raw payloads\nand immutable artifacts are content-addressed. Everything above the kernel builds on these two\nprimitives, so they come first and alone.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA property test renames a node's `canonical_name` a thousand times and its `NodeId` never\nchanges, and the same canonical bytes produce the same `ContentHash` on every run and across the\nSQLite and file providers' serialisation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `crates/ekr-kernel/src/identity.rs` — the id newtypes of `systems/ekr/domains/kernel.yaml`\n  (`AgentId`, `TransactionId`, `RevisionId`, `IssueId`), `ontology.yaml` (`TypeId`, `PropertyId`,\n  `SchemaVersionId`) and `graph.yaml` (`GraphRootId`, `NodeId`, `EdgeId`, `AssertionId`,\n  `SupportId`, `EvidenceId`, `ObservationId`), each a `u128` newtype minted as UUIDv7, with serde\n- `crates/ekr-kernel/src/hash.rs` — `ContentHash([u8; 32])`, SHA-256, hex display\n- `crates/ekr-kernel/src/canonical.rs` — a `Canonical` trait: the deterministic byte encoding a\n  hash is computed over; `BTreeMap` ordering, no floats in keys\n- `crates/ekr-kernel/src/lib.rs`\n\n## Notes\n\nDesign § 10 leaves the scheme open (\"UUIDv7, content-derived identifiers where appropriate\");\nUUIDv7 for minted ids, content-derived for observations and evidence (which are what they hash).\nNothing in this story names a graph concept beyond the id types.\n","title":"Stable identity and content hashing"},"args":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"## Context\n\nDesign § 6.4 and § 10: human-readable names are not identities; every persistent object carries a\nstable id that survives renames, aliases, merges and schema migration. Design § 57: raw payloads\nand immutable artifacts are content-addressed. Everything above the kernel builds on these two\nprimitives, so they come first and alone.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA property test renames a node's `canonical_name` a thousand times and its `NodeId` never\nchanges, and the same canonical bytes produce the same `ContentHash` on every run and across the\nSQLite and file providers' serialisation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `crates/ekr-kernel/src/identity.rs` — the id newtypes of `systems/ekr/domains/kernel.yaml`\n  (`AgentId`, `TransactionId`, `RevisionId`, `IssueId`), `ontology.yaml` (`TypeId`, `PropertyId`,\n  `SchemaVersionId`) and `graph.yaml` (`GraphRootId`, `NodeId`, `EdgeId`, `AssertionId`,\n  `SupportId`, `EvidenceId`, `ObservationId`), each a `u128` newtype minted as UUIDv7, with serde\n- `crates/ekr-kernel/src/hash.rs` — `ContentHash([u8; 32])`, SHA-256, hex display\n- `crates/ekr-kernel/src/canonical.rs` — a `Canonical` trait: the deterministic byte encoding a\n  hash is computed over; `BTreeMap` ordering, no floats in keys\n- `crates/ekr-kernel/src/lib.rs`\n\n## Notes\n\nDesign § 10 leaves the scheme open (\"UUIDv7, content-derived identifiers where appropriate\");\nUUIDv7 for minted ids, content-derived for observations and evidence (which are what they hash).\nNothing in this story names a graph concept beyond the id types.\n","status":"draft","title":"Stable identity and content hashing"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/kernel-identity-and-hashing"},"payload":{"actor":"agent:claude","at":1789955944568,"causation":"cmd-new-story-kernel-identity-and-hashing","change":{"change":"created","status":"draft"},"correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","event_id":"story:kernel-identity-and-hashing@1#0~8a6f1ab651a25fb0","executor":null,"recorded_at":"2026-09-21T01:59:04Z"}}